102
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:39,379
Next is angioedema.

103
00:03:39,379 --> 00:03:42,020
Angioedema is swelling of

104
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:44,979
the deeper dermal and
subcutaneous tissues

105
00:03:44,979 --> 00:03:47,939
of the mouth,
lips, tongue.

106
00:03:47,939 --> 00:03:50,540
When we start to
get angioedema of

107
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:51,940
the lower airway that can

108
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,980
lead to airway compromise.

109
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:56,299
There are two subtypes.

110
00:03:56,299 --> 00:03:58,619
The first is a
hereditary variant,

111
00:03:58,619 --> 00:04:01,019
it's autosomal dominant
and it's due to

112
00:04:01,019 --> 00:04:04,219
a C one esterase
inhibitor deficiency.

113
00:04:04,219 --> 00:04:06,179
The second type
of angioedema

114
00:04:06,179 --> 00:04:07,980
is acquired and it's due

115
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:11,190
to angiotensin
converting enzyme

116
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,629
or ACE inhibitors,

117
00:04:12,629 --> 00:04:14,350
which are a very

118
00:04:14,350 --> 00:04:16,909
common anti
hypertensive medication

119
00:04:16,909 --> 00:04:20,110
and NSAIDs.

120
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:22,309
A little bit about the

121
00:04:22,309 --> 00:04:24,189
pathophys and what's
going on here,

122
00:04:24,189 --> 00:04:27,510
I've attached a picture
of the pathway.

123
00:04:27,510 --> 00:04:30,550
Essentially, in angioedema,
what's happening

124
00:04:30,550 --> 00:04:32,509
is that increased
bradykinin

125
00:04:32,509 --> 00:04:33,814
is what's causing it.

126
00:04:33,814 --> 00:04:35,360
So in the case of

127
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,879
C one sterse
inhibitor deficiency,

128
00:04:37,879 --> 00:04:41,719
if you look at the left
side of this pathway,

129
00:04:41,719 --> 00:04:44,320
C one esterase inhibitor

130
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:47,319
allows for regulated
bradykinin.

131
00:04:47,319 --> 00:04:49,159
So when we have a
deficiency in that,

132
00:04:49,159 --> 00:04:49,919
that will actually

133
00:04:49,919 --> 00:04:51,799
lead to increased
bradyinin

134
00:04:51,799 --> 00:04:54,599
and can potentially
lead to angioedema.

135
00:04:54,599 --> 00:04:57,959
With ACE inhibitors, they

136
00:04:57,959 --> 00:05:00,959
also ACE helps contribute

137
00:05:00,959 --> 00:05:02,839
to the degradation
of bradykinin.

138
00:05:02,839 --> 00:05:05,439
So ACE inhibitors stop

139
00:05:05,439 --> 00:05:07,360
the degradation
of bradykinin.

140
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,560
Again, we have that
increased bradyokin

141
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:12,759
that could potentially
lead to an angioedema.

142
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:15,389
So the way to manage

143
00:05:15,389 --> 00:05:17,189
entry angioedema is going

144
00:05:17,189 --> 00:05:19,109
to be through
early intubation.

145
00:05:19,109 --> 00:05:21,869
You don't want to
wait until the airway

146
00:05:21,869 --> 00:05:23,349
fully collapses and then

147
00:05:23,349 --> 00:05:25,510
it's very hard
to intubate.

148
00:05:25,510 --> 00:05:27,190
You want to make
sure you're

149
00:05:27,190 --> 00:05:28,669
proactive with
these patients.

150
00:05:28,669 --> 00:05:32,749
You want to maintain
an 02 saturation

151
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:34,470
of greater than 90%,

152
00:05:34,470 --> 00:05:37,264
so you want to be mindful
of monitoring that.

153
00:05:37,264 --> 00:05:38,860
And after that, you're

154
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:40,379
going to want to
determine the cause.

155
00:05:40,379 --> 00:05:42,099
If it's due to
a medication,

156
00:05:42,099 --> 00:05:43,339
let's say the patients

157
00:05:43,339 --> 00:05:44,620
taking an ACE inhibitor,

158
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:45,259
you want to make sure

159
00:05:45,259 --> 00:05:46,699
to discontinue
that medication.

160
00:05:46,699 --> 00:05:49,619
If they also have
urticaria present,

161
00:05:49,619 --> 00:05:51,379
it's possible
that they had

162
00:05:51,379 --> 00:05:53,260
a potential
allergic trigger,

163
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,419
so you can consider

164
00:05:54,419 --> 00:05:56,099
administering
antihistamines,

165
00:05:56,099 --> 00:05:58,375
glucorticoids,
and epinephrine.

166
00:05:58,375 --> 00:06:01,129
If the patient has a
hereditary variant

167
00:06:01,129 --> 00:06:02,890
that's causing
this angioedema,

168
00:06:02,890 --> 00:06:04,409
there are certain
medications

169
00:06:04,409 --> 00:06:06,009
that can be used.

170
00:06:06,009 --> 00:06:08,129
A catban is

171
00:06:08,129 --> 00:06:10,290
a bradykin
receptor inhibitor

172
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:11,289
that can be used.

173
00:06:11,289 --> 00:06:14,970
Acenide is a
Kalcrine inhibitor,

174
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:15,769
which is also going

175
00:06:15,769 --> 00:06:18,009
to help decrease
bradykinin.

176
00:06:18,009 --> 00:06:18,889
You can also use

177
00:06:18,889 --> 00:06:21,250
C one esterase
inhibitor and replenish

178
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:24,369
that and you're at

179
00:06:24,369 --> 00:06:25,449
a hospital that doesn't

180
00:06:25,449 --> 00:06:27,050
have these types
of resources,

181
00:06:27,050 --> 00:06:28,569
fresh frozen plasma is

182
00:06:28,569 --> 00:06:30,769
something that you
could also consider.

183
00:06:32,450 --> 00:06:35,449
Before discharge
of the patient,

184
00:06:35,449 --> 00:06:37,889
towards the end of
their hospital stay,

185
00:06:37,889 --> 00:06:41,610
if the patient presented
with an anaphylaxis,

186
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:42,329
you're going to want to

187
00:06:42,329 --> 00:06:43,130
make sure you prescribe

188
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:45,649
an auto injector
epinephrine and give

189
00:06:45,649 --> 00:06:47,849
them education and
counseling on how

190
00:06:47,849 --> 00:06:50,530
to use that auto injector.

191
00:06:50,530 --> 00:06:52,490
If you've identified
a trigger,

192
00:06:52,490 --> 00:06:53,929
you're going to want
again to counsel

193
00:06:53,929 --> 00:06:56,369
and educate your
patient on how

194
00:06:56,369 --> 00:06:58,329
to avoid those
allergens and

195
00:06:58,329 --> 00:07:01,809
triggers to avoid
this situation.

196
00:07:02,290 --> 00:07:04,769
Basically, these
patients are all

197
00:07:04,769 --> 00:07:07,810
getting admitted
into the ICU.

198
00:07:09,410 --> 00:07:12,050
Here we have some pictures

199
00:07:12,050 --> 00:07:14,529
of what angioedema
could look like.

200
00:07:14,529 --> 00:07:16,450
You get the
severe swelling

201
00:07:16,450 --> 00:07:17,849
of the mouth region,

202
00:07:17,849 --> 00:07:19,129
the mouth, the tongue,

203
00:07:19,129 --> 00:07:21,129
and there's probably
also swelling in

204
00:07:21,129 --> 00:07:25,330
that lower airway
causing airway collapse.

205
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:30,800
Next we have
erythema multiforma.

206
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:33,799
This is a type
of rash that

207
00:07:33,799 --> 00:07:37,120
90% of the time is
caused by infections.

208
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,520
The most common of which

209
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,319
is herpes simplex virus.

210
00:07:40,319 --> 00:07:42,359
That's the number one
infectious cause.

211
00:07:42,359 --> 00:07:47,120
The second cause can be
mycoplasma pneumonia.

212
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,800
About 10% of
erythema multiforme

213
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,039
is going to be caused
by some kind of a drug.

214
00:07:52,039 --> 00:07:55,039
Um, so this develops
usually secondary to

215
00:07:55,039 --> 00:07:58,080
a herpes simplex
virus infection via

216
00:07:58,080 --> 00:08:01,400
cell mediated immune
response directed

217
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,039
at viral antigens that

218
00:08:03,039 --> 00:08:05,439
are deposited in
the lesion skin.

219
00:08:05,439 --> 00:08:07,960
This is a clinical
diagnosis

220
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:09,520
like most rashes are,

221
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,159
but what you're
really going to see

222
00:08:11,159 --> 00:08:13,240
are those
targetoid lesions

223
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:15,399
with a central
dusky appearance

224
00:08:15,399 --> 00:08:17,759
is how they're
commonly described.

225
00:08:17,759 --> 00:08:20,319
Erythema multiforma can be

226
00:08:20,319 --> 00:08:23,879
divided into
minor or major.

227
00:08:23,879 --> 00:08:27,079
So if it's erythema
multiforma minor,

228
00:08:27,079 --> 00:08:28,999
it's usually without or

229
00:08:28,999 --> 00:08:31,534
with very mild
mucosal disease.

230
00:08:31,534 --> 00:08:33,989
And without any
associated symptoms

231
00:08:33,989 --> 00:08:35,310
and resolves easily.

232
00:08:35,310 --> 00:08:38,350
But if they have severe
mucosal involvement

233
00:08:38,350 --> 00:08:41,350
and potential systemic
symptoms like a fever,

234
00:08:41,350 --> 00:08:43,789
conjunctivitis, colitis,

235
00:08:43,789 --> 00:08:45,549
that would be
considered erythea

236
00:08:45,549 --> 00:08:47,670
multiforming major.

237
00:08:47,910 --> 00:08:50,870
The symptoms could be

238
00:08:50,870 --> 00:08:53,229
malaise, low grade fever,

239
00:08:53,229 --> 00:08:54,750
and then those targoid

240
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:56,350
lesions are going
to develop over

241
00:08:56,350 --> 00:08:57,990
several days and
they're going to be

242
00:08:57,990 --> 00:09:01,119
painful and
pariic or itchy.

243
00:09:01,119 --> 00:09:02,850
So the lesions and

244
00:09:02,850 --> 00:09:04,730
erythema multiforma
are going

245
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:06,690
to appear over the course

246
00:09:06,690 --> 00:09:07,929
of three to five days,

247
00:09:07,929 --> 00:09:10,730
specifically in the
palms and soles.

248
00:09:10,730 --> 00:09:12,650
They can spread outside

249
00:09:12,650 --> 00:09:13,850
of that as well, though.

250
00:09:13,850 --> 00:09:15,409
The lesions typically are

251
00:09:15,409 --> 00:09:16,210
going to resolve within

252
00:09:16,210 --> 00:09:17,650
14 days and they're

253
00:09:17,650 --> 00:09:19,129
usually not going to scar,

254
00:09:19,129 --> 00:09:19,970
but they can be

255
00:09:19,970 --> 00:09:22,170
hyperpigmented
for a few months.

256
00:09:22,170 --> 00:09:25,130
You can treat
erythema multiforme

257
00:09:25,130 --> 00:09:26,690
with antivirals if you

258
00:09:26,690 --> 00:09:28,570
find that the cause of

259
00:09:28,570 --> 00:09:31,329
this was herpes
simplex virus.

260
00:09:31,329 --> 00:09:34,530
You can also use
acyclovir to

261
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:38,019
prevent recurrence of
erythema multiforme.

262
00:09:38,019 --> 00:09:41,189
If the cause of this
was drug induced,

263
00:09:41,189 --> 00:09:42,550
then you're just going
to want to avoid

264
00:09:42,550 --> 00:09:43,869
drugs in the future.

265
00:09:43,869 --> 00:09:45,470
You'll consider systemic

266
00:09:45,470 --> 00:09:47,230
steroids if it's severe

267
00:09:47,230 --> 00:09:49,990
and a dermatology consult

268
00:09:49,990 --> 00:09:51,870
as with most of
these rashes.

269
00:09:51,870 --> 00:09:53,470
You'll also want
to provide your

270
00:09:53,470 --> 00:09:55,790
patient with
